Chapter: DeskPillEdgeTest
  cites Works chapter GopDraw
  cites Works chapter GopDesk
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 ShellRefinement 6.7.1. A pill's edge is a per-app fact, keyed by focus id,
 defaulting to the band's own edge until something writes one. Damian ruled
 the flick's DIRECTION the selection criterion on 2026-08-27; this is the
 place the direction will be spent, and this stage lands it inert.

 THE INERTNESS IS THE CLAIM AND IT IS THE HALF WORTH ASSERTING. Nothing writes
 an entry yet, so every pill must still answer the band's edge at all four
 edges. A row that only checked "a written value comes back" would pass with
 the default broken, and a row that only checked the default would pass if the
 block were never allocated at all -- so both are here and they fail for
 different reasons.

 ZERO IS THE TRAP. `alloc-zeroed` hands back zeros and `dk-edge-bottom` is 0,
 so an unwritten slot and a slot flicked to the bottom are the same bits unless
 the stored value is offset. The row that discriminates is **writing
 `dk-edge-bottom` explicitly and requiring it to survive a band whose edge is
 something else**: with a raw store that reads back as the band's edge and the
 defect is invisible at the default geometry.

Section: Body

  dpe-yn : Boolean -> Text
  dpe-yn (v) = if v then "yes" else "NO"

  dpe-defaults : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Text
  dpe-defaults (ds) (e) (i) =
    if i >= dk-pedge-slots then "all default to the band"
    else if dk-pedge-get ds i /= e then "id " & integer-to-text i & " answered " & integer-to-text (dk-pedge-get ds i) & " not " & integer-to-text e
    else dpe-defaults ds e (i + 1)

  dpe-row : Integer, Integer -> Text
  dpe-row (ds) (e) =
    let sp = poke-32 ds dk-task-edge-cell e
    in "edge " & dk-edge-name e
       & "  band " & integer-to-text (dk-task-edge ds)
       & "  unwritten id 3 " & integer-to-text (dk-pedge-get ds 3)
       & "  default follows band " & dpe-yn (dk-pedge-get ds 3 == e)
       & "  " & dpe-defaults ds e 0

 A WRITE MUST SURVIVE, AND THE ONE THAT DISCRIMINATES IS `dk-edge-bottom`
 WRITTEN UNDER A BAND THAT IS NOT AT THE BOTTOM. The other three edges would
 read back correctly even from a raw store.

  dpe-write : Integer -> Text
  dpe-write (ds) =
    let sp = poke-32 ds dk-task-edge-cell dk-edge-top
    in let a = dk-pedge-set ds 5 dk-edge-bottom
    in let b = dk-pedge-set ds 6 dk-edge-left
    in "band top, wrote bottom to id 5 and left to id 6"
       & "  id 5 " & integer-to-text (dk-pedge-get ds 5)
       & "  survives " & dpe-yn (dk-pedge-get ds 5 == dk-edge-bottom)
       & "  id 6 " & integer-to-text (dk-pedge-get ds 6)
       & "  survives " & dpe-yn (dk-pedge-get ds 6 == dk-edge-left)
       & "  untouched id 7 still band " & dpe-yn (dk-pedge-get ds 7 == dk-edge-top)

 OUT OF RANGE ANSWERS THE BAND RATHER THAN READING PAST THE BLOCK. The block
 is `dk-pedge-slots` entries and `dk-focus-max` is 16, so id 16 is the last
 valid one and 17 is the first that must be refused.

  dpe-bounds : Integer -> Text
  dpe-bounds (ds) =
    let sp = poke-32 ds dk-task-edge-cell dk-edge-right
    in "out of range: id -1 " & integer-to-text (dk-pedge-get ds (0 - 1))
       & "  id 17 " & integer-to-text (dk-pedge-get ds 17)
       & "  both answer the band " & dpe-yn (dk-pedge-get ds (0 - 1) == dk-edge-right & dk-pedge-get ds 17 == dk-edge-right)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing =
    let ds = alloc-zeroed 256 64
    in let ap = poke-32 ds dk-adorn-cell dk-adorn-default
    in let pei = dk-pedge-init ds
    in act
      print-line-uni (dpe-row ds dk-edge-bottom)
      print-line-uni (dpe-row ds dk-edge-top)
      print-line-uni (dpe-row ds dk-edge-left)
      print-line-uni (dpe-row ds dk-edge-right)
      print-line-uni (dpe-write ds)
      print-line-uni (dpe-bounds ds)
    end

